                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A wonderfully atmospheric reimagining that seamlessly blends classic deduction with clever mechanical innovations for a highly rewarding puzzle experience.\n\nIf you are thinking of picking up this particular hidden-object adventure, it is an exceptionally well-crafted title that breathes fresh life into a classic Victorian gothic tale. While purists might be surprised by its bold narrative swings, the execution delivers an engaging loop of smart puzzle design, immersive environments, and specialized gameplay mechanics that make uncovering the dark family curse a true joy.\n\nHere is what you need to know before diving in:\n\n• Cleverly Integrated Hidden-Object Scenes: Hunting for clues never feels artificial or tedious. Key items are intricately woven directly into the hand-drawn backgrounds, matching the visual geometry of the ancestral estate naturally so you are scanning logically rather than pixel-hunting blindly.\n\n• Supernatural Medallion Abilities: Progression avoids stagnant item combinations by giving the detective an interactive artifact. Over the course of the mystery, you unlock distinct character abilities—like Telekinesis, Strength, and Perception—which change how you manipulate environmental obstacles on the fly.\n\n• Moorland Time-Travel Mechanics: The game introduces a brilliant supernatural twist allowing you to jump between the past and present within specific rooms. This adds a fascinating layer to your deduction, letting you see the immediate aftermath of historical crimes to piece together family secrets across generations.\n\n• Atmospheric Presentation and Pacing: The cursed mansion feels appropriately cold, cheerless, and steeped in gothic horror. Backed by an excellent, moody soundtrack and high-quality voice acting, the world keeps you eager to push forward through its 35+ beautifully detailed locations.\n\nFinal Verdict: A standout puzzle adventure that replaces genre friction with genuinely creative mechanics. If you want a beautifully atmospheric gothic mystery with great puzzle variety and a fast-travel system that respects your time, do not skip out on this unique, supernatural spin on the World's Greatest Detective.",
